# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Node
node_modules/
# the repo's own lock stays local (single dev dep); the examples' locks stay TRACKED (they pin the worked reference projects)
/package-lock.json

# Windows
Thumbs.db

# claude
.claude/
# this repo's own data root when a worktree carries no settings (hook receipts, docs state)
/.alfred/
REPORT.md

# Stack-generated, machine-local artifacts (never commit)
.serena/
.mcp.json

# local research input (contains private project names) - never commit
best-practice/
docs/session-to-analize/
docs/session-investigation/
# ...and every near-spelling of it: a 115MB collection of real transcripts sat in
# `docs/sessions-investigation/` (plural) where the exact line above did not reach it, one
# `git add -A` away from a public repo. The glob is the containment, not the exact name.
docs/*investigation*/

# examples: worked reference projects - track clean source, exclude build caches,
# stack state, and grader-only harness artifacts. (node_modules/.claude/.serena/.mcp.json/
# .vscode/REPORT.md/.DS_Store are already ignored globally above.)
examples/**/.angular/
examples/**/.playwright/
examples/**/dist/
examples/**/bin/
examples/**/obj/
examples/**/*.db
examples/**/*.db-wal
examples/**/*.db-shm
examples/ANSWER-KEY.md
examples/*ANSWER-KEY*.md
examples/*-test-prompt.md
examples/RUN-*PHASES*.md
examples/**/RETEST-REPORT.md
examples/**/VERIFY-REPORT.md

# docs: the committed architecture map (docs/architecture/) + repo docs stay tracked; only the
# superpowers / brainstorming scratch specs are local-only.
**/docs/superpowers/

# .superpowers/: the subagent-driven-development workspace - ledger, task briefs, implementer and
# review reports. The tooling that writes it treats it as git-ignored scratch, and it names absolute
# local paths, so in a PUBLIC repo one `git add -A` away from committing them. Ignored, not tracked:
# the durable record of a plan is its commits, not the reports that argued for them.
.superpowers/

# docs/usefull/: locally saved copies of third-party pages (token-optimization articles, the
# official best-practices page) read by the audits - reference material, never redistributed.
docs/usefull/

# setup-plugin/evals/: the cases and graders are tracked; a RUN's output is machine-local and
# large (per-run transcripts plus a self-contained HTML report), and every run re-dates its
# directory - the number worth keeping is the with / without delta, which goes in the eval
# README, not the artifact.
setup-plugin/evals/results/
